{"t": 1795766431.19, "stage": "critic", "msg": "Mathematics: All forty keys check out on recomputation, and the spread across coordinate geometry, calculus, algebra, vectors/3D and probability is broadly syllabus-appropriate, though integral calculus (109, 110, 113, 127) and sets/functions (97, 103, 107, 128) are slightly over-weighted. The level is uneven: several items are single-step recall (101, 113, 124, 130) while 109, 114 and 127 are JEE-style problems that could exceed the 90-second budget, especially 114 where the two extraneous roots at $\\pi/2$ and $3\\pi/2$ must be discarded. Fix the two typographical/wording slips and swap one heavy definite-integral item for a moderate one to even out the section.", "level": "info"}
